# The cgui-workspace scene's scratch project. Real files the user edits; not build output,
# which is why it is not under harness-output/ -- but not source either.
#
# ANCHORED. Unanchored, `workspace/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, so
# src/main/resources/harness/workspace -- the seeds this scratch project is created FROM -- was
# ignored along with it. A source file that git silently refuses to track is the worst half of that:
# it works locally forever and is missing for everybody else.
/workspace/

# A DESKTOP ARRANGEMENT IS THIS MACHINE'S, not the scene's. `cgui-desktop` persists where you
# left every window, and its own javadoc says "with no record at all it does nothing, so a first run
# looks exactly as it always has" -- which is only true if nobody ships one. The session record beside
# it is tracked deliberately (it is a fixture other scenes read); this is state.
/workspace-config/desktop.*.json
